WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.960
I think we both met Chris
Farley around the same time.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.620
I remember very clearly when
he came to Saturday Night Live.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.775
And he was waiting for
an interview with Lorne

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:10.608
and I think he had

00:00:10.608 --> 00:00:12.820
to wait for two days
outside Lorne's office.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.610
And so I ended up just
clowning around with

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:19.380
this great new guy I'd never
met before named Chris Farley.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.790
You met him probably shortly

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.973
after he was hired for
Saturday Night Live.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.346
Because you knew Lorne
you knew Lorne Michaels.

00:00:27.346 --> 00:00:28.179
Yes

00:00:28.179 --> 00:00:29.690
So how did you is that when you met Chris,

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.230
'cause I know you
eventually worked with him

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.063
in Tommy Boy,

00:00:32.063 --> 00:00:35.317
but you met him I think at
Lauren's house is that correct?

00:00:35.317 --> 00:00:37.730
I met him I met him at Lauren's wedding,

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:41.570
and how you there's certain people in life

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:44.220
that for whatever reason you
remember exactly where you were

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.730
when you met them.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.520
And think about many people
that we meet famous not famous,

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.500
and we don't remember where
we met them for the first time

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.570
or what they were doing
or how they were standing.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.510
Farley was one of those guys,

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.790
probably because he was
packed into a suit that

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.833
was 17 times too small for him.

00:00:58.833 --> 00:00:59.666
Right.

00:00:59.666 --> 00:01:02.423
And sweat Like he had
jumped into Lake Michigan,

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:05.600
but he was standing by the porta potties.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.490
And then of course his first
acting job in a movie was

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:12.450
in Wayne's World 2.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.310
And then of course we
did Tommy Boy together

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:15.940
and I loved him.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.743
He was funny and he and Spade.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.070
they would fight over me
like I was the hot girl.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:23.960
They were they would
get very jealous of who

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.660
was spending time with me.

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:27.550
And it really made me laugh.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.383
I understand that.

00:01:28.383 --> 00:01:31.007
I get where they're coming from.

00:01:31.007 --> 00:01:33.768
I really understand that.

00:01:33.768 --> 00:01:36.260
I'm always jealous when I hear

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.850
that you're spending time with others.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:42.790
And one quick Farley story
is he loved to eat steak.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:47.310
And I took him to a steak house
when we wrapped Tommy Boy,

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:52.310
and he had two full bone in Porter houses.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:58.070
Upon each bite of the two
full bonus edge Porter houses,

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:01.423
he put an entire cube of butter,

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.550
on every bite.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:08.690
And when I was horrified like
Farley what are you doing,

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.789
he said it needs a hat.

00:02:11.789 --> 00:02:16.789
(laughs)

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.030
Oh God bless him.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.560
Yes, what a brilliantly funny guy.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:27.914
I've never I've never
eaten steak, every bite

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.360
of steak I eat to this day.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.237
I go I wonder if I
should put a hat on this.

00:02:32.237 --> 00:02:34.440
(laughs)
Maybe not,

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.960
Surgeon General might disagree.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:36.793
Yeah
No.

